  "infoSummaryCopy": "INFO — field reference\n• USB-C = shape, not speed: check the standard.\n• NVMe (M.2) is much faster than SATA.\n• DisplayPort/HDMI = standards, watch versions/cables.\n• On video servers: storage + GPU + bandwidth are the base.",

  "infoChecklistCopy": "INFO — Checklist\n☐ Certified USB-C cables (data/video if needed)\n☐ Suitable storage (NVMe for heavy media)\n☐ Stable GPU drivers (known version)\n☐ Real resolution/FPS test\n☐ Avoid cheap adapters",

  "infoUsbCriticalTitle": "Critical point",
  "infoUsbCriticalBullet1": "USB-C = connector (shape). It does not indicate speed.",
  "infoUsbCriticalBullet2": "A USB-C cable can be “charge only” and not carry data/video.",

  "infoUsbSpeedTitle": "Speed reference points (rough order of magnitude)",
  "infoUsbSpeedBullet1": "USB 2.0: slow (keyboards, dongles, small peripherals).",
  "infoUsbSpeedBullet2": "USB 3.x: much faster (drives, interfaces).",
  "infoUsbSpeedBullet3": "USB4 / Thunderbolt: very high bandwidth (dock, eGPU, video depending on hardware).",
  "infoUsbParagraph": "In show conditions: if a peripheral misbehaves, suspect the cable (quality/standard) before the device.",

  "infoStorageSataNvmeTitle": "SATA vs NVMe",
  "infoStorageSataNvmeBullet1": "SATA SSD: good and stable, but limited (older interface).",
  "infoStorageSataNvmeBullet2": "NVMe SSD (M.2): much faster (ideal for media servers, large files).",

  "infoStorageFieldTitle": "Video field use",
  "infoStorageFieldBullet1": "Playback of large 4K/ProRes files → NVMe recommended.",
  "infoStorageFieldBullet2": "Watch temperature: an NVMe can throttle (slow down) if it gets hot.",
  "infoStorageFieldBullet3": "Always test under real conditions before the show.",

  "infoVideoLinksImportantTitle": "Important point",
  "infoVideoLinksImportantBullet1": "Versions matter: cable + port + device must all be compatible.",
  "infoVideoLinksImportantBullet2": "Long distance = active converters / fiber often required.",

  "infoVideoLinksCompareTitle": "DP vs HDMI (very simplified)",
  "infoVideoLinksCompareBullet1": "HDMI: everywhere (TVs, processors), but EDID/HDCP can get in the way.",
  "infoVideoLinksCompareBullet2": "DisplayPort: very common on PCs, often very capable in bandwidth.",

  "infoPcieGpuParagraph": "For video servers / mapping: GPU + bus + drivers = stability. Typical issues: drivers, cables, conversion, and output limitations.",
  "infoPcieGpuFieldTitle": "Field",
  "infoPcieGpuFieldBullet1": "Lock a stable driver version before a major show.",
  "infoPcieGpuFieldBullet2": "Avoid cheap adapters.",
  "infoPcieGpuFieldBullet3": "Test at the real show resolution/FPS.",

  "infoChecklistQuickTitle": "Quick",
  "infoChecklistBullet1": "Correct cable/standard.",
  "infoChecklistBullet2": "Storage suited to the media flow.",
  "infoChecklistBullet3": "Stable drivers.",
  "infoChecklistBullet4": "Real-world test before show.",
  "infoChecklistBullet5": "Avoid cheap adapters.",

  "infoFooterNote": "Indicative field information. Exact capabilities vary depending on hardware/versions.\nGoal: simple reference points + reliable method.",

  "ipBasicsPageTitle": "Network — IP basics / mask / DHCP (essential)",
  "ipBasicsCopyMemoTooltip": "Copy memo",
  "ipBasicsCopyChecklistTooltip": "Copy checklist",

  "ipBasicsMemo1": "IP = logical address used to reach a device on a network.",
  "ipBasicsMemo2": "Private (LAN): 10.x.x.x, 172.16–31.x.x, 192.168.x.x (not routed on the Internet).",
  "ipBasicsMemo3": "Mask / subnet = tells which part is “network” vs “host”.",
  "ipBasicsMemo4": "Same subnet = direct communication. Otherwise → gateway (router).",
  "ipBasicsMemo5": "DHCP assigns IP automatically; static = useful for nodes/console.",

  "ipBasicsToc1": "1) What is an IP address and what is it for?",
