  "aboutNetworkBasicsPill1": "Dedicated/VLAN",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsPill2": "Wired",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsPill3": "IGMP if multicast",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsParagraph": "A lighting network must be predictable: low loss, low jitter, simple architecture. When it breaks, it is rarely “the protocol” and often the infrastructure (switch, Wi-Fi, loops, flood).",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsCalloutTitle": "Basic rule",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsBullet1": "If possible: wired + proper switch + dedicated network (or VLAN).",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsBullet2": "If you must share: VLAN + clear rules.",
  "aboutNetworkBasicsBullet3": "sACN multicast: IGMP quickly becomes mandatory.",

  "aboutNetworkPlanIpParagraph": "Choose a simple and coherent strategy. Two approaches: DHCP (simple) or static (predictable). The worst option: an undocumented mix.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpCalloutTitle": "Example plan (simple)",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet1": "Lighting VLAN: 10.10.0.0/24",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet2": "Console/PC: 10.10.0.10",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet3": "Nodes: 10.10.0.100–150",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpBullet4": "Switch mgmt: 10.10.0.2",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubtitle": "Common mistakes",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubBullet1": "Different mask (ex: /24 vs /16) → devices become invisible.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubBullet2": "Two devices with the same IP → random behavior.",
  "aboutNetworkPlanIpSubBullet3": "DHCP + static on the same range without control → conflicts.",

  "aboutNetworkVlanParagraph": "A VLAN lets you isolate lighting from everything else (internet, video production, guests…). This reduces network noise and the risk that another service breaks your show.",
  "aboutNetworkVlanCalloutTitle": "What you gain",
  "aboutNetworkVlanBullet1": "Less parasite traffic.",
  "aboutNetworkVlanBullet2": "Less risk (external DHCP, unwanted broadcast).",
  "aboutNetworkVlanBullet3": "Simpler debugging (everything in the VLAN = lighting).",
  "aboutNetworkVlanSubtitle": "Warning",
  "aboutNetworkVlanSubBullet1": "A VLAN means all ports must be configured correctly (access/trunk).",
  "aboutNetworkVlanSubBullet2": "If you do not master it: a dedicated physical network is often simpler.",

  "aboutNetworkIgmpPill1": "IGMP snooping",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpPill2": "IGMP querier",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpPill3": "Multicast flood",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpParagraph": "IGMP snooping lets the switch know which ports want which multicast. Without it, multicast can be flooded to every port → saturation.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpCalloutTitle": "IGMP querier (simple idea)",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpBullet1": "In some networks/VLANs, a querier is needed to maintain IGMP subscriptions.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpBullet2": "Without a querier: depending on the switches, subscriptions expire and you get “glitches”.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpBullet3": "On a small dedicated network: everything may work, but on a large network: it becomes critical.",
  "aboutNetworkIgmpSubtitle": "Diagram: IGMP (concept)",

  "aboutNetworkWifiSubtitle1": "Wired",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubtitle2": "Wi-Fi",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet1": "✅ Stable latency, low loss (if infrastructure is clean).",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet2": "✅ Recommended in production.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet3": "✅ Convenient (quick setup, tablet).",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet4": "❌ Variable latency (jitter), losses, interference.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet5": "❌ Multicast sometimes poorly handled depending on AP/config.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiSubBullet6": "OK for troubleshooting / small non-critical setups, rarely OK on a busy show.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiCalloutTitle": "Simple rule",
  "aboutNetworkWifiBullet1": "Critical show = wired.",
  "aboutNetworkWifiBullet2": "Wi-Fi = operator comfort (UI), not main DMX/IP transport for heavy traffic.",

  "aboutNetworkSwitchCalloutTitle": "Recommended minimum",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet1": "Proper Ethernet switch (not a hub).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet2": "Good cables (RJ45, connectors).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet3": "Avoid loops (or controlled STP).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchBullet4": "For sACN multicast: IGMP snooping.",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchSubtitle": "Managed vs unmanaged",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchSubBullet1": "Unmanaged: OK for a small dedicated network (simple).",
  "aboutNetworkSwitchSubBullet2": "Managed: useful for VLAN/IGMP/diagnostics (larger network).",

  "aboutNetworkDiagramsSubtitle1": "VLAN: separate lighting / everything else",
  "aboutNetworkDiagramsSubtitle2": "Wi-Fi vs wired (concept)",

  "aboutNetworkChecklistBullet1": "Clear IP plan, coherent mask.",
  "aboutNetworkChecklistBullet2": "Dedicated network / lighting VLAN.",
  "aboutNetworkChecklistBullet3": "Switch OK, no loops.",
  "aboutNetworkChecklistBullet4": "IGMP for sACN multicast.",
  "aboutNetworkChecklistBullet5": "Avoid Wi-Fi in critical production.",

  "aboutReseauPageTitle": "Network — field reference",
  "aboutReseauSummaryCopy": "NETWORK — field reference\n• RJ45: Cat5e/6/6A → 1G/10G depending on distance.\n• Fiber: long distance + EMI immunity.\n• Switch: IGMP matters for sACN multicast.\n• VLAN: separating lighting/video/IT = stability.",
  "aboutReseauChecklistCopy": "NETWORK — Checklist\n☐ Clear IP plan (range / masks)\n☐ Proper switch (IGMP if sACN multicast)\n☐ VLAN if several “worlds” (lighting/video/IT)\n☐ Tested + labeled cables\n☐ Fiber: compatible modules + clean connectors\n☐ Avoid loops (STP) + avoid public Wi-Fi on show LAN",
  "aboutReseauChecklistCopyTooltip": "Copy",
  "aboutReseauFooterNote": "Indicative field info. Exact capabilities vary depending on hardware / cables / modules.\nGoal: simple reference points + reliable method.",

  "aboutReseauToc1": "1) Network basics (LAN / IP / bandwidth)",
  "aboutReseauToc2": "2) RJ45 & categories (Cat5e/6/6A/…)",
  "aboutReseauToc3": "3) PoE (network power)",
  "aboutReseauToc4": "4) Fiber (SM/MM) + connectors (LC/SC)",
  "aboutReseauToc5": "5) SFP / SFP+ / QSFP (modules)",
  "aboutReseauToc6": "6) Switches (VLAN / IGMP / QoS)",
  "aboutReseauToc7": "7) Art-Net / sACN on network (tips)",
  "aboutReseauToc8": "8) Checklist",

  "aboutReseauSection1Title": "The 3 simple ideas",
  "aboutReseauSection1Bullet1": "IP = address (ex: 10.0.0.50).",
  "aboutReseauSection1Bullet2": "LAN = local network through a switch (not “internet”).",
  "aboutReseauSection1Bullet3": "Bandwidth = capacity (1G, 10G…), but stability also depends on the switch.",
  "aboutReseauSection1Title2": "Clean show topology",
  "aboutReseauSection1Bullet4": "Console/PC → central switch → nodes/servers.",
  "aboutReseauSection1Bullet5": "Avoid random network daisy-chains.",
  "aboutReseauSection1Bullet6": "If possible: a dedicated show network (not public Wi-Fi).",

  "aboutReseauSection2Title": "Quick reference points",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet1": "Cat5e: classic 1 Gbit/s (up to 100m).",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet2": "Cat6: 1G/10G (10G rather on shorter distances).",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet3": "Cat6A: 10G up to 100m (practical reference).",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet4": "Beyond that: Cat7/8 exist, but Cat6A is often the field sweet spot.",
  "aboutReseauSection2Title2": "Field",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet5": "Always test/label cables (especially rentals).",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet6": "Avoid damaged connectors: a “tired” RJ45 = ghost faults.",
  "aboutReseauSection2Bullet7": "Plan for 10G if you do heavy IP video.",

  "aboutReseauSection3Paragraph": "PoE allows devices to be powered over RJ45 (IP cameras, Wi-Fi APs, small nodes…). The critical point is the switch’s total PoE budget.",
  "aboutReseauSection3Title": "Reference points",
  "aboutReseauSection3Bullet1": "PoE (802.3af) ≈ 15W, PoE+ (802.3at) ≈ 30W, PoE++/bt higher.",
  "aboutReseauSection3Bullet2": "The switch has a total “budget” (ex: 120W).",
  "aboutReseauSection3Bullet3": "If you exceed the budget: some ports may stop powering / reboot.",

  "aboutReseauSection4Title": "Why fiber in show environments",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet1": "Very long distances.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet2": "Immunity to interference (EMI), excellent in electrically noisy environments.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet3": "Convenient for linking FOH ↔ stage ↔ control room.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Title2": "Multimode vs Singlemode (simple reference)",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet4": "Multimode (MM): “medium” distances (often building / stage).",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet5": "Singlemode (SM): very long distances.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet6": "Modules (SFP) must match the fiber type.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Title3": "Connectors",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet7": "LC: small, very common on SFP.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet8": "SC: larger, common in infrastructure.",
  "aboutReseauSection4Bullet9": "Always protect/clean them (dust = losses).",

  "aboutReseauSection5Title": "Reference points",
  "aboutReseauSection5Bullet1": "SFP: often 1G.",
  "aboutReseauSection5Bullet2": "SFP+: often 10G.",
  "aboutReseauSection5Bullet3": "QSFP/QSFP+: 40G (depending on usage).",
  "aboutReseauSection5Bullet4": "A module = speed + fiber type + distance (everything must match).",
